      "common:shortName": [],
      "common:generalComment": [
        {
          "#text": "An alloy is a mixture of chemical elements, at least one of which is a metal. Alloys have different properties from pure metals, such as strength, hardness, conductivity, and corrosion resistance. They are formed by melting two or more elements together, at least one of them metal. An alloy crystallizes upon cooling into a solid solution, mixture, or intermetallic compound. The components of alloys cannot be separated using physical means.",
          "@xml:lang": "en"
        },
        {
          "#text": "合金是化学元素的混合物，其中至少有一种是金属。合金具有与纯金属不同的特性，如强度、硬度、导电性和耐腐蚀性。合金是将两种或两种以上的元素熔化在一起形成的，其中至少有一种元素是金属。合金冷却后会结晶成固溶体、混合物或金属间化合物。合金的成分无法用物理方法分离。",
          "@xml:lang": "zh"
        }
      ],
